-- title:
--   Occupancy and rank factorisation of the Σ-corner at level Mr
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be an absolutely irreducible two-dimensional residual Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal O$. Fixed data: a finite set $S$ of primes containing $p$; a level $M$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2\nmid M$; a subset $Smin\subseteq S$ containing $p$ which away from $p$ consists exactly of the primes where $\bar\rho$ is ramified, together with the divisibility conditions relating $Smin$ to $M$ ($q\mid M$ for $q\in Smin$, $q\neq p$; $q^2\mid M$ for primes $q\neq p$ dividing $M$ outside $Smin$; no $q^3\mid M$), unipotence of $\bar\rho$ on inertia at the primes of $Smin$ away from $p$ and ordinarity at $p$ when $p\mid M$; an auxiliary prime $r\notin S$ with $r\nmid M$, $p\nmid r-1$, such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $r$ a nonunit in $P$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ one has $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$; a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ to the residue field whose values at $T_\ell$ give the characteristic polynomials $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ of the Frobenii of $\bar\rho$ at primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$; and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_T$ from the localisation $\mathrm{heckeLocal}$ of the base-changed Hecke algebra at the kernel prime of $\theta$ to $\mathcal O$. Let $L=Mr$ and let $H\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $r$, and let $\mathbb T$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite over $\mathcal O$, acting on $H^1(L,H,\mathcal O)=\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{ad}},\mathcal O)$ compatibly with $\mathcal O$. Let $Sp$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ with their maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_j$) and $i$ an index such that the corner submodule $e_i\cdot H^1(L,H,\mathcal O)$ is finite and free over $\mathcal O$. Further data: families $tfull$, $cfull$ on the generators $T_\ell$, $U_q$, $\langle d\rangle$ at level $L$ away from $S$, subject to: every element of $\mathbb T$ acts on $H^1$ by an element of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the operators $\mathrm{opFamily}$ attached to the generators $g$ satisfying the guard that $g=U_q$ forces $q\mid M$; $tfull\,g$ acts as $\mathrm{opFamily}\,g$ for guarded $g$; $tfull\,g-cfull\,g\in\mathfrak m_i$; a vector of $H^1$ lies in the corner submodule as soon as, for all guarded $g$ and all $k$, some power of $tfull\,g-cfull\,g$ carries it into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k H^1$; the residue of $cfull(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell\nmid L$, $\ell\notin S$; $cfull(U_q)$ lies in the maximal ideal when $q\mid M$, $q\neq p$, $q^2\mid M$; $cfull(U_p)$ is a unit when $p\mid M$; $cfull(\langle d\rangle)\equiv 1$. Finally assume the corner submodule is nonzero, the corner ring $e_i\mathbb Te_i$ acts faithfully on it, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from the corner ring to $\mathrm{heckeLocal}$ is given which carries $T_\ell$ to the Hecke operator $\mathrm{heckeT}\,L\,H\,\ell$ on the corner submodule for all $\ell\nmid L$, $\ell\notin S$. The conclusion is twofold: the submodule of elements of the corner submodule annihilated by every element of $\ker(\pi_T\circ e)$ is nonzero, and the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner submodule equals the $\mathcal O$-rank of that torsion submodule times the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner ring.
--
--   This is the occupancy-and-rank statement for the $\Sigma$-shaped corner of the Hecke action on degree-one group cohomology at the auxiliary level $L=Mr$: the $\pi_T$-eigencomponent is nonzero and the corner module is, in rank, free over the corner ring. It supplies the level-raising rung at $p$ and is used by the packaging results [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_cornerData_unitRoot_refinement_package_level_mul_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_cornerData_unitRoot_refinement_package_level_mul_of_not_cube_dvd) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_pairing_eq_bfam_sigmaResidue_guarded`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_pairing_eq_bfam_sigmaResidue_guarded).
